Spoilers ahead...


If you're chaotic, #offer corpses at an altar.  This will sometimes land
you Stormbringer, among other goodies.  Since Stormbringer is a choatic
weapon, only a chaotic God will bestow it at an altar.

As for wishing, here is the list I keep a printout of near my computer.
Clip and save!


     "blessed +3 war hammer named Mjollnir"
     "blessed +3 broadsword named Stormbringer"
     "blessed +3 katana named Snickersnee"
     "blessed +3 long sword named Excalibur"
     "blessed +3 gray dragon scale mail"
     "blessed +3 helm of telepathy"
     "blessed +3 pair of speed boots"
     "blessed +3 gauntlets of power"
     "blessed +3 shield of reflection"
     "blessed +3 cloak of displacement"
     "blessed +3 Hawaiian shirt"
     "blessed amulet of life saving"
     "3 blessed potions of gain ability"
     "3 blessed scrolls of genocide"
     "3 cursed scrolls of genocide" (caution is advised)
     "blessed spellbook of identify" (you never get more than one spellbook)
     "blessed ring of levitation"
     "wand of polymorph"
     "blessed tinning kit" (makes blessed tins)
     "figurine of a gray dragon" (for that pet gray dragon you always wanted)

These are the exact spellings, from the Spoilers.

Remember that you will not always get what you ask for.  The way
I understand it, there are so many "points" allowed in a wish.  It
may have to do with your luck and prayer status, or it may be just
random.  But "points" are counted in a wish if you desire a "blessed"
item or a "+" item.  The most you are allowed is a blessed +3 item.
I've wished for a "blessed +3 long sword named Excalibur" and received
a plain blessed Excalibur, without the +3.  Go figure...

Also, remember that an Excalibur received through wishing will not be
rustproof.  I don't believe you can wish for a rustproofed item either.
There are other ways of doing that.

